\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces Full vs, most restricted rows of data for the model with start of season (SOS; a) and end of season (EOS; b) as the predictor. Each panel represent the different parameters used to fit the models. $\alpha _{species}$ and $\alpha _{year}$ represent the ring width (log(mm)) for species and year, respectively. $\beta _{species}$ represent the change in ring width (log(mm)) per scaled predictor for each species (see `Data analyses' section in Methods for more details on predictor scaling).}}{46}{figure.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
